        "step_number": 1,
        "text": "Step 1: We start by examining the given recurrence relation for \\( f(n+1) \\):\n\\[ f(n + 1) = (-1)^{n + 1} n - 2f(n). \\]"
      },
      {
        "aligned_char_end": 243,
        "boundary_aligned_back": true,
        "char_end": 245,
        "char_start": 120,
        "effective_step": 2,
        "end_token_index": 82,
        "near_end": false,
        "prefix_token_count": 83,
        "step_number": 2,
        "text": "Step 2: To find a pattern, we calculate the first few terms of the sequence using the initial condition \\( f(1) = f(1986) \\)."
      },
      {
        "aligned_char_end": 324,
        "boundary_aligned_back": true,
        "char_end": 325,
        "char_start": 247,
        "effective_step": 3,
        "end_token_index": 127,
        "near_end": false,
        "prefix_token_count": 128,
        "step_number": 3,
        "text": "Step 3: Calculate \\( f(2) \\):\n\\[ f(2) = (-1)^2 \\cdot 1 - 2f(1) = 1 - 2f(1). \\]"
      },
      {
        "aligned_char_end": 442,
        "boundary_aligned_back": true,
        "char_end": 443,
        "char_start": 327,
        "effective_step": 4,
        "end_token_index": 200,
        "near_end": false,
        "prefix_token_count": 201,
        "step_number": 4,
        "text": "Step 4: Calculate \\( f(3) \\):\n\\[ f(3) = (-1)^3 \\cdot 2 - 2f(2) = -2 - 2(1 - 2f(1)) = -2 - 2 + 4f(1) = -4 + 4f(1). \\]"
      },
      {
        "aligned_char_end": 559,
        "boundary_aligned_back": true,
        "char_end": 560,
        "char_start": 445,
        "effective_step": 5,
        "end_token_index": 274,
        "near_end": false,
        "prefix_token_count": 275,
        "step_number": 5,
        "text": "Step 5: Calculate \\( f(4) \\):\n\\[ f(4) = (-1)^4 \\cdot 3 - 2f(3) = 3 - 2(-4 + 4f(1)) = 3 + 8 - 8f(1) = 11 - 8f(1). \\]"
      },
      {
        "aligned_char_end": 708,
        "boundary_aligned_back": true,
        "char_end": 709,
        "char_start": 562,
        "effective_step": 6,
        "end_token_index": 314,
        "near_end": false,
        "prefix_token_count": 315,
        "step_number": 6,
        "text": "Step 6: Notice that the terms alternate in sign and involve multiples of \\( f(1) \\). Let's hypothesize a general form for \\( f(n) \\) and verify it."
      },
      {
        "aligned_char_end": 1123,
        "boundary_aligned_back": true,
        "char_end": 1124,
        "char_start": 711,
        "effective_step": 7,
        "end_token_index": 505,
        "near_end": false,
        "prefix_token_count": 506,
        "step_number": 7,
        "text": "Step 7: Assume \\( f(n) = a_n f(1) + b_n \\), where \\( a_n \\) and \\( b_n \\) are sequences to be determined. From the recurrence relation, we can derive:\n\\[ f(n+1) = (-1)^{n+1} n - 2f(n). \\]\nSubstituting \\( f(n) = a_n f(1) + b_n \\) into the recurrence:\n\\[ a_{n+1} f(1) + b_{n+1} = (-1)^{n+1} n - 2(a_n f(1) + b_n). \\]\nThis gives us two equations:\n\\[ a_{n+1} f(1) = (-1)^{n+1} n - 2a_n f(1), \\]\n\\[ b_{n+1} = -2b_n. \\]"
      },
      {
        "aligned_char_end": 1243,
        "boundary_aligned_back": true,
        "char_end": 1245,
        "char_start": 1126,
        "effective_step": 8,
        "end_token_index": 567,
        "near_end": false,
        "prefix_token_count": 568,
        "step_number": 8,
        "text": "Step 8: Solve for \\( b_n \\):\n\\[ b_{n+1} = -2b_n. \\]\nSince \\( b_1 = 0 \\) (from \\( f(1) = f(1986) \\)), all \\( b_n = 0 \\)."
      },
      {
        "aligned_char_end": 1371,
        "boundary_aligned_back": true,
        "char_end": 1372,
        "char_start": 1247,
        "effective_step": 9,
        "end_token_index": 642,
        "near_end": false,
        "prefix_token_count": 643,
        "step_number": 9,
        "text": "Step 9: Solve for \\( a_n \\):\n\\[ a_{n+1} f(1) = (-1)^{n+1} n - 2a_n f(1), \\]\n\\[ a_{n+1} = (-1)^{n+1} \\frac{n}{f(1)} - 2a_n. \\]"
      },
      {
        "aligned_char_end": 1761,
        "boundary_aligned_back": true,
        "char_end": 1762,
        "char_start": 1374,
        "effective_step": 10,
