        "near_end": false,
        "prefix_token_count": 866,
        "step_number": 10,
        "text": "Step 10: We observe that the sum of the series \\( f(1) + f(2) + \\cdots + f(1985) \\) can be simplified by pairing terms. Notice that:\n\\[ f(2k-1) + f(2k) = (-1)^{2k-1} (2k-1) - 2f(2k-1) + (-1)^{2k} 2k - 2f(2k) = -(2k-1) + 2k - 2(f(2k-1) + f(2k)). \\]\nThis simplifies to:\n\\[ f(2k-1) + f(2k) = 1 - 2(f(2k-1) + f(2k)). \\]\nThus,\n\\[ 3(f(2k-1) + f(2k)) = 1, \\]\n\\[ f(2k-1) + f(2k) = \\frac{1}{3}. \\]"
      },
